# What NOT to upload on a local `vercel deploy`.
#
# Deploys normally happen from git, where only tracked files exist and this file is
# irrelevant. It matters for the escape hatch: `vercel deploy` from this machine uploads the
# working directory, and the first attempt died with "File size limit exceeded (100 MB)"
# because it swept in `_local/` (150 MB of the owner's private notes and scratch files).
# Being gitignored was not enough, so the exclusions are restated here.

# Owner's private working folder. Big, and none of Vercel's business.
_local/

# Regenerated locally by `graphify update .`
graphify-out/

node_modules/
.git/
.vercel/

# Never ship secrets. The build reads env vars from the platform, not from a file.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Local build output: Vercel builds from source.
pwa/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Historical archive, kept in the repo for reference, useless at runtime.
n8n/

# Docs and process files the running app never reads.
docs/
project-board/
specs/
knowledge/_raw/
